      ⍝ one more: sum overflows int64, promoted to float
      ⍝
      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #11a, 2026-08-06): the two
      ⍝ overflow tests below (and the negative-boundary pair further down)
      ⍝ used to compute a+b (here and in Subtract.tc's a-b) *before*
      ⍝ checking for overflow -- signed overflow is UB, so a compiler
      ⍝ would have been entitled to assume it never happens and delete
      ⍝ the float fallback. IntCell::bif_add_ii()/bif_subtract_ii() now
      ⍝ compute via uint64_t (well-defined wraparound) first.
      ⍝
      9223372036854775807+1
9.2233720368547758E18
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2
      26⎕CR 9223372036854775807+1
32
      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP

